# Critical Rules (NO EXCEPTIONS)

- **npm only** — never pnpm or yarn
- **Schema first**: always check `database/schema.sql` before any SQL; never assume column names
- **Never edit `database/schema.sql` directly for schema changes** — write a migration in `database/migrations/` first, apply it, then update `schema.sql` to match
- **API monolith**: all required API logic stays **inline** in `api/index.ts` (Vercel serverless). Do **not** runtime-import from `shared/` in the API — `import type` only. Shared runtime modules break prod with `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND`
- **Redux only for data**: never axios/fetch in components; use `createAsyncThunk` in slices; components only dispatch + select
- **Fix root causes** — never patch around type errors or bugs
- **No breaking changes**
- **Swagger (always with API changes)**: any change to `api/index.ts` routes, request/response shapes, or behavior → **update `api/swagger.yaml` in the same change**
- **DESIGN_SYSTEM.md (always with UI/brand/email/flow changes)**: any change to visuals, branding, email templates, public pages, or product flows → **update `DESIGN_SYSTEM.md` in the same change**
- **i18n (always)**: every user-visible string in `client/` MUST use `t('key')` via `useTranslation()` — never hardcode UI copy. Add the same key to BOTH `client/locales/en/translation.json` AND `client/locales/es/translation.json` in the same change. Browser language is detected (`navigator` + `localStorage`); **fallback language is English**. Yup/Formik messages are i18n keys too.
- **Tests & local QA: never send real notifications.** `VITEST=true` must never send live Resend email, Twilio SMS, Ably publishes, or in-app `admin_notifications` to real staff — staff fan-out in tests is limited to `@example.com` / `@example.test` fixtures. Integration tests that write to TiDB must clean fixtures in `afterAll` using `api/testDbCleanup.ts` (only `@example.com` / `@example.test`). Enforced in code by `notifySandbox()` in `api/index.ts` (on for every Vitest run): email / SMS / Ably are dry-run and staff fan-out skips non-test admins. Manual QA on the dev server delivers for real unless you set `NOTIFY_SANDBOX=true` in `.env` — always do that before QA, and only use `@example.com` fixtures. New outbound channels MUST check `notifySandbox()`.
- **Review chat history** before changing code so you do not reintroduce fixed issues
- Prefer reusable components/utilities when it avoids debt
- **Mobile (mandatory — see `.cursor/rules/mobile-responsive.mdc`):** public + portal + admin UI must fit ~320px+ with **no document horizontal scroll** (vertical scroll only at page level). Contain intentional sideways scroll in wrappers (`overflow-x: auto` + `max-width: 100%`). Fluid layouts, `min-width: 0`, collapsing grids, wrapping actions. Fix overflowing children — do not hide bugs with body `overflow-x: hidden` alone. Validate at ~320px and ~375px before finishing any UI work.
- Frontend: clean UX; UI logs via `client/utils/logger.ts`
